---
import {backlog,rates} from './movement.mjs';
---
<figure aria-labelledby="r30-catchup-title">
  <figcaption id="r30-catchup-title"><span>Figure 2</span> Catch-up needs a surplus over new changes</figcaption>
  <div class="chart">
    <p>Initial backlog: 600 MiB · new history: 40 MiB/s · compare after 10 seconds</p>
    <p class="scale">Bar scale: 0–800 MiB of unprocessed history</p>
    <div class="row"><strong>At start</strong><div class="track"><span style="width:75%"></span></div><p>600 MiB behind</p></div>
    {rates.map(rate=><div class="row"><strong>Apply {rate} MiB/s</strong><div class="track"><span style={`width:${backlog(rate)/8}%`}></span></div><p>{backlog(rate)} MiB behind after 10 s{rate===30?' · growing':rate===60?' · shrinking':' · caught up'}</p></div>)}
  </div>
  <p class="caption">Constant-rate arithmetic for an already installed snapshot, with identical units for incoming and applied history. At 60 MiB/s the 20 MiB/s surplus would clear 600 MiB in 30 seconds; at 100 MiB/s the 60 MiB/s surplus clears it in 10. These are illustrative calculations, not measured database throughput or an operational completion estimate. Copying, stalls, compaction, protocol work and changes in traffic are excluded.</p>
</figure>
<style>
 figure{margin:2.5rem 0}figcaption{font:1.25rem/1.4 var(--font-serif);margin-bottom:.8rem}figcaption>span{font:.75rem var(--font-sans);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin-right:.6rem}.chart{padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);font:.85rem/1.5 var(--font-sans)}.chart>p{margin:0 0 .7rem}.scale{color:var(--color-text-secondary)}.row{padding:.8rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary)}.row p{margin:.25rem 0 0}.track{width:100%;height:1rem;background:var(--color-surface-alt);border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);margin-top:.4rem}.track span{display:block;height:100%;background:var(--color-accent)}.caption{font:.85rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);color:var(--color-text-secondary)}
</style>
